{"type": "rna_memory_snapshot", "memdir": "/data/wenhui/openclaude_rna/rna_harness/runs/m2p_scale/seeded_diverse/memdir_seeded_diverse/", "memory_md_path": "/data/wenhui/openclaude_rna/rna_harness/runs/m2p_scale/seeded_diverse/memdir_seeded_diverse/MEMORY.md", "injected": true, "sha256": "ed76ad15f86efad59c3c5b6bc7b509e3905c920319801af1089078892ca7e173", "n_chars": 624, "n_lines": 10, "content": "# RNA design playbook (learned strategies)\n\n- Cap each hairpin with a stable 4-nt tetraloop, but VARY the loop across adjacent hairpins. Stable\n  choices include GAAA, UUCG, GCAA, GAGA, CUUG, GGAA \u2014 rotate through them so neighbouring hairpins\n  do NOT share the same loop sequence.\n- Close helices with strong pairs but ALTERNATE the orientation (G-C on one helix, C-G on the next;\n  an occasional A-U/U-A is fine) to break sequence repetition between hairpins.\n- Why: repeated identical loops + identical stems create spurious cross-hairpin base pairs that\n  misfold the whole assembly. Diversity across units is the key.\n", "memdir_md_files": ["MEMORY.md"], "note": "openclaude injects ONLY MEMORY.md into the agent system prompt; other files in memdir are present but not auto-injected by default."}
